    "subtopic": "Integration by Parts",
    "difficulty": "MODERATE",
    "stem": "Find \\(\\int \\log x \\, dx\\).",
    "solution": "We cannot guess a function whose derivative is \\(\\log x\\). Take \\(\\log x\\) as the first function and the constant function \\(1\\) as the second function; the integral of the second function is \\(x\\). Hence \\(\\int (\\log x \\cdot 1)\\, dx = \\log x \\int 1\\, dx - \\int [\\frac{d}{dx}(\\log x) \\int 1\\, dx]\\, dx = (\\log x)\\cdot x - \\int \\frac{1}{x}\\, x \\, dx = x \\log x - x + C\\)."
  },
  {
