    "format": "subjective",
    "subtopic": "Integration by Parts",
    "difficulty": "EASY",
    "stem": "Find \\(\\int x\\, e^{x} \\, dx\\).",
    "solution": "Take the first function as \\(x\\) and the second function as \\(e^{x}\\). The integral of the second function is \\(e^{x}\\). Therefore \\(\\int x\\, e^{x} \\, dx = x\\, e^{x} - \\int 1 \\cdot e^{x} \\, dx = x e^{x} - e^{x} + C\\)."
