    "stem": "Find \\(\\int e^{x}\\left(\\tan^{-1} x + \\frac{1}{1+x^{2}}\\right) dx\\).",
    "solution": "We have \\(I = \\int e^{x}\\left(\\tan^{-1} x + \\frac{1}{1+x^{2}}\\right) dx\\). Consider \\(f(x) = \\tan^{-1} x\\), then \\(f'(x) = \\frac{1}{1+x^{2}}\\). Thus the integrand is of the form \\(e^{x}[f(x) + f'(x)]\\), and \\(\\int e^{x}[f(x)+f'(x)]\\, dx = e^{x} f(x) + C\\). Therefore \\(I = e^{x} \\tan^{-1} x + C\\)."
